From: qyYue1389 <qyYue1389@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 04:17:46 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 11/19] feat(rl): GFlowRL policy loss (arXiv:2607.13394 Eq.
 4-8), C-prime variant

Two halves, per P7_ROUTE_C_PLAN:

- ray_trainer.compute_gflowrl_flow_gap(): the gradient-free half. Eq. 4
  in-batch log Z estimate over the uid group, Eq. 6 flow gap, Eq. 7
  asymmetric clip. Broadcasts g~ into batch['advantages'].
- core_algos.compute_policy_loss_gflowrl(): the gradient-carrying half,
  registered as loss_mode 'gflowrl'. Eq. 8 with a stop-gradient IS weight.

The 'variant' switch selects where |y| normalization is applied:
  paper      Eq.4 unnormalized, Eq.5/6 normalized (as published)
  normalized both normalized
  cprime     neither  <- what we train with

Only cprime has the Prop. B.1 analytic fixed point once lengths are
ragged; verified to 7.4e-13 by tools/p7/p7_fixedpoint_check.py, which
extracts these two functions from source rather than reimplementing
them. paper and normalized both saturate the clip and land at loss
~4-5e-2 at the exact fixed point. See records/P7_ROUTE_C_GATE.md and
records/P7_STEP_C12_RESULTS.md.

masked_sum (not masked_mean) in the policy term is load-bearing and
silent if changed: it is the whole difference between cprime and
normalized. Guard: run p7_fixedpoint_check.py after touching either
function.

Also warns (never raises) when response_mask looks like the
ray_trainer.py:157 attention-mask fallback, which would silently fold
tool-response tokens into |y|.

Inert unless actor.policy_loss.loss_mode == 'gflowrl'.

